+# Release 1.5.5: precise timing moves (any amount, whole transcript or one line)
+
+This release builds on 1.5.4 (Sync, Timings toggle, Paste text, shared timing fixes), which is described further down.
+
+**What changes in 1.5.5**
+
+- The ±1 s / ±5 s buttons are gone. Type **any amount in seconds** (decimals work, for example 0.5 or 2.25) and tap **◀ Earlier** or **Later ▶**.
+- **The move applies to the whole transcript by default.** Tap a line (in Sync mode) to choose it; then the move applies to **only that line**, or switch to **This line and after**. Tap the line again, or **Whole transcript**, to go back. Moves add up, and opposite moves cancel. **Reset all** clears everything.
+- A **Play** button on each line (in Sync mode) jumps playback to that line, so you can check it.
+- Moves are saved for everyone on your server for server-generated transcripts, like the Set fixes. Times are shown to the second, so very small moves only show once they add up to a full second.
+
+| Question (1.5.5 only) | Answer |
+| --- | --- |
+| New database migration? | **No.** The moves are stored inside the existing `transcript_edits` table from 1.5.4 (migration `0004_transcript_timing.sql`, which must already be applied; the script applies it if not). |
+| Worker deployment? | **Yes.** An old Worker would drop the new kind of move when saving. |
+| Android release? | **Yes.** |
+
+---
+
